 "text": "Monday, Japan tries something no spacecraft has ever done: bring home a piece of a Martian moon.  The mission is MMX, and it is headed for Phobos.  The plan?  orbit Phobos, land, scoop up a sample, and fly it back to Earth.  the first material ever returned from the Mars system.  Why?  Nobody knows where Mars got its two moons. A sample could crack that.  It even carries a tiny French and German rover called Idafix.  Liftoff is Monday, October 19, on an H-III rocket.  We will show you the launch.",
